## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a beginner PCA pipeline in a cross-tenant setting with latency constraints and interpret loadings for cohort definitions. Emphasizes data cleaning, scaling, component retention strategy, and practical mapping from components to business actions.

## Key Concepts
- PCA basics: imputation, scaling, centering
- Global vs per-tenant PCA; explained variance threshold
- Loadings interpretation; cohort definition
- Latency considerations: batch vs streaming; incremental options

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode illustrating preprocessing and PCA call
function buildPCA(data) {
  const imputed = imputeMeanPerFeature(data);
  const scaled = scaleToUnitVariance(imputed);
  // assume PCA is available and returns components/loadings
  const pca = new PCA(scaled, {nComponents: 6});
  return pca.loadings;
}
```

```javascript
// Example interpretation
const top = pcaLoadings[0];
console.log(top); // { sessions_per_week: 0.68, content_views: 0.52, ... }
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor stability of the 6 components across weeks?
- How would you adjust if the explained variance dips below the target over time?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design streaming PCA with drift, privacy, and governance integration at scale.

## Key Concepts

- Online Incremental PCA, mini-batch updates, drift detection
- Streaming imputation, feature scaling, memory budgeting
- Differential privacy in streaming aggregation, per-tenant sharing
- Loadings interpretation and governance alert mapping

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton of streaming online PCA update
function update(batch) {
  const X = impute(batch);
  const Xs = scale(X);
  components = incrementalPCA(components, Xs, k);
  const loadings = components.loadings;
  publish(loadings);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to set drift-detection thresholds in production?
- How to allocate privacy budget over time?
